{
  "tema": 5599,
  "slug": "construyo-huyo",
  "titulo": "Huir and construir in the present",
  "subtitulo": "Construyo un gallinero; el gato huye.",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "Verbs ending in -uir (huir, construir, destruir, incluir…) add a y before the ending in the present: construyo, huyes, incluye, construyen. Nosotros has no y: construimos, huimos.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In the present, verbs ending in **-uir** add a **y** after the **u** in every person **except nosotros**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "huir",
            "construir"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "huyo",
              "construyo"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "huyes",
              "construyes"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "huye",
              "construye"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros / nosotras",
              "huimos",
              "construimos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "huyen",
              "construyen"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Nosotros** is regular: **construimos**, **huimos** (the ending starts with **i**, so no y is needed)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The same pattern works for all **-uir** verbs: **destruir**, **incluir**, **concluir**, **contribuir**, **distribuir**, **sustituir**, **influir**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It does **not** apply to **-guir** verbs, where the u is silent: **seguir → sigo**, **conseguir → consigue**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the **y** is a little bridge between the u and the vowel that follows. Nosotros already has an **i**, so it doesn't need the bridge."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Este fin de semana ==construyo== una cama elevada para los jitomates.",
              "en": "This weekend I'm building a raised bed for the tomatoes."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los gatos ==huyen== cuando llega el perro del vecino.",
              "en": "The cats run away when the neighbor's dog shows up."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nosotros ==construimos== un gallinero en la azotea.",
              "en": "We're building a chicken coop on the roof."
            },
            {
              "es": "El precio ==incluye== la renta de la tabla.",
              "en": "The price includes the board rental."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Por qué ==huyes== de tus problemas?",
              "en": "Why do you run away from your problems?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Las olas grandes ==destruyen== los castillos de arena.",
              "en": "Big waves destroy the sandcastles."
            },
            {
              "es": "En la novela, los cinturianos ==construyen== una estación enorme.",
              "en": "In the novel, the Belters build a huge station."
            },
            {
              "es": "Dormir bien ==contribuye== mucho a tu progreso en el tatami.",
              "en": "Sleeping well contributes a lot to your progress on the mat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
